Description: build, sign and install custom Linux kernels
 KernelCustom Manager is a GTK4/libadwaita application for Debian that
 makes custom kernels easy:
  - download kernel sources from kernel.org and configure them;
  - compile them into Debian packages (make bindeb-pkg) and install them;
  - manage the sources in /usr/src (links for DKMS);
  - install GPU drivers (Debian repositories, or the official NVIDIA
    installer);
  - SecureBoot: create and enroll a MOK key, sign the modules and the
    kernel image;
  - clean up the working directory.
 .
 Privileged operations go through a helper with a whitelist of actions,
 authorized by PolicyKit.
